session:pr737 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:717 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-10-30T19:54:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-30T19:54:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr737Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #717 was a follow-up from a memory-cost review of #701/#683: DerivedFromIndex::by_rule (a rule_id -> derived-quad reverse index, added so negation_invalidated_seeds could avoid an O(total derivations) scan) unconditionally indexed every rule_id that ever produced a recorded derivation, even though negation_invalidated_seeds only ever looks up rule_ids that negatively_triggered_rules has already matched -- i.e. rule_ids with a NOT body atom. For a program with many purely-positive rules (the common case), by_rule was paying roughly double DerivedFromIndex's memory for rule_ids that could never actually be queried. Checked the provenance record for #701 first (per the task's provenance-check step) to confirm by_rule's original design intent and its B/F-paper lineage before touching it. Added a negatively_triggering_rules: HashSet<usize> field to DerivedFromIndex, computed once in DatalogProgram::new (in the same loop that already builds neg_rule_map, so no extra pass over the rule set) and updated via a new mark_negatively_triggering call in add_rule for rules added after construction. record() now only writes into by_rule when the derivation's rule_id is in that set; decrement_by_rule/remove needed no changes since they already no-op gracefully on a rule_id with no by_rule entry. No other call site (the three other derived_from.record calls in incremental.rs) needed changes, since they all operate on a DatalogProgram already built via new/add_rule." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:737 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr737Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr737 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr737Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Computed the negatively-triggering rule_id set inside DatalogProgram::new/add_rule (where neg_rule_map is already built) and passed it into DerivedFromIndex via a constructor/mark method, rather than filtering inside DerivedFromIndex::record by having the index somehow discover which rule_ids are negatively-triggering on its own." ;
    agp:alternative "Having DerivedFromIndex itself inspect Rule bodies to determine which rule_ids are negatively-triggering was rejected: DerivedFromIndex (datalog/src/types.rs) has no dependency on Rule/RuleAtom's NotPattern variant or on DatalogProgram, and introducing one just to re-derive a set DatalogProgram::new already computes while building neg_rule_map would be a needless coupling in the wrong direction -- the issue itself asked for exactly this split (caller computes/passes the set, index just uses it)." .
